description: Synchronize reader and Learn work at verified checkpoints without disturbing active edits
alwaysApply: true
---

# Workstream synchronization

- The user delegates routine reader/Learn coordination and sync timing to the
  ChatGPT learning workstream. Inspect the code and live GitHub state first.
- Choose a coherent, committed and verified milestone as the sync boundary.
  Do not pull, rebase, switch, stash or reset over another agent's active edits.
- Use one coordinator for each shared-baseline handoff. Other agents checkpoint
  their work and hold shared edits until that coordinator confirms completion.
- Rehearse integration in an isolated checkout when work is concurrent. Pin
  exact input commits. Pending PR heads are preview inputs, not released code.
- Preserve both workstreams at shared boundaries: reader conversations and
  annotations, Learn drafts and evidence, document schema compatibility, app
  entry points and model selection. Add a joint regression for a real conflict.
- Run the combined relevant checks; separate green branches do not establish
  compatibility. Retain the recorded limits of native UI verification.
- Resolve routine integration conflicts while preserving agreed behavior.
  Escalate conflicting product decisions to the relevant owners and user.
- Coordinate Git-index use before adopting the verified result. Never publish
  unreleased Learn code as an incidental reader update, or infer authorization
  for a release, force-push or history rewrite from routine synchronization.
- Keep exact inputs, resolutions and checks in repository evidence, and update
  the corresponding Linear item. Notify other agents of the new baseline.
